  "content": {
    "id": "p20-q1-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "1",
    "prompt": "Suppose $p$ and $q$ are the roots of quadratic $x^2-3x-6$. Find the values of:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p20-q1-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$p+q$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$3$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}p+q&=-\\frac{b}{a}\\\\p+q&=-\\frac{-3}{1}\\\\p+q&=3\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q1-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$pq$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-6$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}pq&=\\frac{c}{a}\\\\pq&=\\frac{-6}{1}\\\\pq&=-6\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q1-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$p^2+q^2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$21$",
          "worked": "By Vieta’s formulas, $p+q=3$ and $pq=-6$.\n$$\\begin{align*}p^2+q^2&=(p+q)^2-2pq\\\\p^2+q^2&=3^2-2(-6)\\\\p^2+q^2&=21\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q1-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac1p+\\dfrac1q$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-\\dfrac12$",
          "worked": "By Vieta’s formulas, $p+q=3$ and $pq=-6$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac1p+\\frac1q&=\\frac{p+q}{pq}\\\\\\frac1p+\\frac1q&=\\frac3{-6}\\\\\\frac1p+\\frac1q&=-\\frac12\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q1-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac pq+\\dfrac qp$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-\\dfrac72$",
          "worked": "By Vieta’s formulas, $p+q=3$ and $pq=-6$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac pq+\\frac qp&=\\frac{p^2+q^2}{pq}\\\\\\frac pq+\\frac qp&=\\frac{(p+q)^2-2pq}{pq}\\\\\\frac pq+\\frac qp&=\\frac{3^2-2(-6)}{-6}\\\\\\frac pq+\\frac qp&=-\\frac72\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 56
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q1-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$p^3+q^3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$81$\n\nUse $p^3+q^3=(p+q)^3-3pq(p+q)$.",
          "worked": "By Vieta’s formulas, $p+q=3$ and $pq=-6$.\n$$\\begin{align*}p^3+q^3&=(p+q)^3-3pq(p+q)\\\\p^3+q^3&=3^3-3(-6)(3)\\\\p^3+q^3&=27+54\\\\p^3+q^3&=81\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      }
    ]
  },
